{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And she sat at the entrance of her house</b> — prepared for disaster, without building a house and without preparation — unlike what he said: 'In wisdom she built her house, she slaughtered her slaughter, she mixed her wine, she even set her table.' The reason: wisdom requires preparation and readiness, but folly does not, for it is the absence of preparation and readiness." "<b>At the seat of the heights of the city</b> — for folly comes by way of pride, and therefore he assigned it a throne. The meaning is like: 'on the wings of.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:44.926480671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}